.TH BENCH 1 "September 2026" "speller-benchmark 2.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
bench \- benchmark a CS50 speller against the staff implementation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bench
[
.BR \-h | \-\-help
]
[
.BR \-v | \-\-version
]
[
.BR \-1 | \-\-single-thread
]
[
.BR \-s | \-\-staff-speller " PATH"
]
[
.BR \-y | \-\-your-speller " PATH"
]
[
.BR \-n | \-\-no-staff
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bench
runs the supplied speller binary against the staff solution over the sample texts
stored in the project\'s
.I texts
directory. It reports timing and correctness data for each file and prints an
aggregate total and average.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h , \-\-help
Show the help text and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v , \-\-version
Print the benchmark version number and exit.
.TP
.BR \-1 , \-\-single-thread
Run the benchmark serially instead of launching one worker thread per text file.
.TP
.BR \-s , \-\-staff-speller " PATH"
Path to the staff speller executable. Defaults to
.IR ./speller50 .
.TP
.BR \-y , \-\-your-speller " PATH"
Path to your speller executable. Defaults to
.IR ./speller .
.TP
.BR \-n , \-\-no-staff
Skip the staff implementation and benchmark only your speller.
.SH EXAMPLES
.B bench --your-speller ./speller --staff-speller ./speller50
.PP
.B bench --single-thread --no-staff
.SH SEE ALSO
The project README for usage notes and expected benchmark output.
